1253 0 obj<</Subtype/Square/Rect[1943 894 2365 1501]/T(AutoCAD SHX Text)/F 64/Contents(REMOVE INTERFACE BETWEEN FIRE ALARM SYSTEM AND ELEVATOR CONTROLLER. PREPARE INTERFACE FOR NEW FIRE ALARM SYSTEM. THE ELEVATOR SHALL BE CONFIGURED TO REMAIN FULLY OPERATIONAL DURING EXISTING FIRE ALARM SYSTEM DEMOLITION AND NEW FIRE ALARM SYSTEM INSTALLATION.   EXISTING 4-WIRE DUCT SMOKE DETECTORS TO REMAIN. REMOVE FIRE ALARM SYSTEM INTERFACE BETWEEN DUCT DETECTOR ALARM CONTACTS AND PREPARE DUCT DETECTOR FOR RE-USE AND INTERFACING WITH NEW FIRE ALARM SYSTEM. EXISTING FIRE SMOKE DAMPERS TO REMAIN. DAMPERS SHALL BE CONFIGURED TO REMAIN OPEN DURING EXISTING FIRE ALARM SYSTEM DEMOLITION AND NEW FIRE ALARM SYSTEM INSTALLATION. DAMPERS WITHIN M/E 126 ARE SERVED BY PNL 1, CKT 12.  REMOVE EXISTING LOCKING HARDWARE AND PREPARE DOOR FOR INSTALLATION OF NEW CARD READER, LOCK, EXIT REQUEST DEVICE AND FIRE ALARM INTERFACE.  REMOVE EXISTING INTRUSION ALARM CONTROL PANEL AND POWER SUPPLIES FROM ROOM 121. REMOVE DEDICATED 120 VAC POWER AND RECONFIGURE FOR NEW EQUIPMENT LOCATION. NO FIRE ALARM, INTRUSION ALARM AND ASSOCIATED POWER SUPPLIES WILL REMAIN IN ROOM 121. PATCH AND PAINT WALLS AND CEILINGS.   REMOVE EXISTING FIRE ALARM CONTROL PANEL AND DISCONNECT FROM DEDICATED 120 VAC POWER. THE FIRE ALARM CONTROL PANEL WILL BE RELOCATED TO ALLOW FOR SLIGHT RECONFIGURATION OF FURNITURE AND CUBICLES. PATCH AND PAINT AS REQUIRED TO ACCOMMODATE NEW ROOM CONFIGURATION AND CONTROL PANEL LOCATION.   REMOVE INTERFACE TO SPRINKLER SYSTEM SUPERVISORY SWITCHES, INCLUDING VALVE TAMPER SWITCHES, WATER FLOW SWITCHES AND PRESSURE SWITCHES. RECONFIGURE EXISTING ROUGH-IN FOR REUSE WITH NEW FIRE ALARM SYSTEM.   REMOVE SPRINKLER SYSTEM WATER FLOW BELL AND RECONFIGURE EXISTING ROUGH-IN FOR REUSE WITH NEW FIRE ALARM SYSTEM. EXISTING CARBON MONOXIDE DETECTOR INSTALLED DURING A RECENT HVAC UPGRADE TO REMAIN.)/Border[0 0 0]/NM(IJCRWBVKAOCKKXWB)/M(D:20250228120642-06'00')/AP<</N 9847 0 R>>/RD[0 0 0 0]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:contentType="text/html" xfa:APIVersion="BluebeamPDFRevu:2018" xfa:spec="2.2.0" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p>REMOVE INTERFACE BETWEEN FIRE ALARM SYSTEM AND ELEVATOR CONTROLLER. PREPARE INTERFACE FOR NEW FIRE ALARM SYSTEM. THE ELEVATOR SHALL BE CONFIGURED TO REMAIN FULLY OPERATIONAL DURING EXISTING FIRE ALARM SYSTEM DEMOLITION AND NEW FIRE ALARM SYSTEM INSTALLATION.   EXISTING 4-WIRE DUCT SMOKE DETECTORS TO REMAIN. REMOVE FIRE ALARM SYSTEM INTERFACE BETWEEN DUCT DETECTOR ALARM CONTACTS AND PREPARE DUCT DETECTOR FOR RE-USE AND INTERFACING WITH NEW FIRE ALARM SYSTEM. EXISTING FIRE SMOKE DAMPERS TO REMAIN. DAMPERS SHALL BE CONFIGURED TO REMAIN OPEN DURING EXISTING FIRE ALARM SYSTEM DEMOLITION AND NEW FIRE ALARM SYSTEM INSTALLATION. DAMPERS WITHIN M/E 126 ARE SERVED BY PNL 1, CKT 12.  REMOVE EXISTING LOCKING HARDWARE AND PREPARE DOOR FOR INSTALLATION OF NEW CARD READER, LOCK, EXIT REQUEST DEVICE AND FIRE ALARM INTERFACE.  REMOVE EXISTING INTRUSION ALARM CONTROL PANEL AND POWER SUPPLIES FROM ROOM 121. REMOVE DEDICATED 120 VAC POWER AND RECONFIGURE FOR NEW EQUIPMENT LOCATION. NO FIRE ALARM, INTRUSION ALARM AND ASSOCIATED POWER SUPPLIES WILL REMAIN IN ROOM 121. PATCH AND PAINT WALLS AND CEILINGS.   REMOVE EXISTING FIRE ALARM CONTROL PANEL AND DISCONNECT FROM DEDICATED 120 VAC POWER. THE FIRE ALARM CONTROL PANEL WILL BE RELOCATED TO ALLOW FOR SLIGHT RECONFIGURATION OF FURNITURE AND CUBICLES. PATCH AND PAINT AS REQUIRED TO ACCOMMODATE NEW ROOM CONFIGURATION AND CONTROL PANEL LOCATION.   REMOVE INTERFACE TO SPRINKLER SYSTEM SUPERVISORY SWITCHES, INCLUDING VALVE TAMPER SWITCHES, WATER FLOW SWITCHES AND PRESSURE SWITCHES. RECONFIGURE EXISTING ROUGH-IN FOR REUSE WITH NEW FIRE ALARM SYSTEM.   REMOVE SPRINKLER SYSTEM WATER FLOW BELL AND RECONFIGURE EXISTING ROUGH-IN FOR REUSE WITH NEW FIRE ALARM SYSTEM. EXISTING CARBON MONOXIDE DETECTOR INSTALLED DURING A RECENT HVAC UPGRADE TO REMAIN.</p></body>)>>
endobj
