1264 0 obj<</Subtype/Square/Rect[126 528 474 1503]/T(AutoCAD SHX Text)/F 64/Contents(1. FIRE-RESISTANT RATED BARRIERS SHALL BE FIRE-RESISTANT RATED BARRIERS SHALL BE MAINTAINED. INSTALL FIRESTOPPING AND JOINT SEALANTS AS REQUIRED FOR NEW THROUGH AND MEMBRANE PENETRATIONS. SEAL ALL PENETRATIONS ABANDONED AS PART OF THE SCOPE OF WORK. 2. THE REINFORCED CONCRETE SHEAR WALL MEASURES THE REINFORCED CONCRETE SHEAR WALL MEASURES 24 INCHES THICK. NO NEW THROUGH PENETRATIONS SHALL BE MADE. EXISTING THROUGH PENETRATIONS AND OPENINGS SHALL BE USED. SURFACE MOUNT DEVICE MOUNTING MAY BE ALLOWED WITH NPS PRIOR APPROVAL. 3. CORRIDOR 101 FEATURES A DYE SUBLIMATION CORRIDOR 101 FEATURES A DYE SUBLIMATION PRINTED PVC PHOTOGRAPHIC FLOOR COVERING SUSCEPTIBLE TO MECHANICAL DAMAGE FROM LADDERS, LIFTS, SCAFFOLDING AND DROPPED TOOLS. CONTRACTOR SHALL PROTECT THE ENTIRE FLOOR WITH ROLLED PAPER BOARD PROTECTOR HAVING A MINIMUM THICKNESS OF 40 MIL. OVERLAP SEAMS BY 6IN AND TAPE SEAMS TOP AND BOTTOM WITH SEAM TAPE SUPPLIED FROM THE SAME MANUFACTURER AS PAPER BOARD. WHERE SELF PROPELLED LIFTS OR SCAFFOLDS ARE USED 1/2IN PLYWOOD PLANKS OR SHEETS SHALL BE PLACED OVER PAPER BOARD TO AFFORD A HIGHER LEVEL OF PROTECTION. 4. COORDINATE ALL WORK WITHIN PUBLIC AREAS COORDINATE ALL WORK WITHIN PUBLIC AREAS \(ROOMS, 100, 101, 102, 103, 105, 106, 111, 112, 113, 114 AND 115\) WITH NPS TO ENSURE THAT WORK DOES NOT IMPACT THE VISITOR'S EXPERIENCE. WORKING AFTER HOURS OR OFF SEASON MAY BE REQUIRED. 5. WORK PERFORMED WITHIN LOWER DISTRICT RESOURCE WORK PERFORMED WITHIN LOWER DISTRICT RESOURCE PROTECTION OFFICES \(RM 119\), STORAGE \(RM 121\), COLLECTION STORAGE \(RM 124\) AND ARCHIVE STORAGE \(RM 125\) MUST BE PERFORMED WITH NPS ESCORT BEING PRESENT. 6. ALL CEILING TILES BROKEN OR OTHERWISE DAMAGED ALL CEILING TILES BROKEN OR OTHERWISE DAMAGED DURING DEMOLITION AND SYSTEM INSTALLATION SHALL BE REMOVED AND REPLACED WITH CEILING TILES TAKEN FROM THE RESOURCE PROTECTION OFFICE \(RM 119 AND 120\). UPON COMPLETION OF DEMOLITION AND INSTALLATION ALL REMAINING CEILING TILES WITHIN THE RESOURCE PROTECTION OFFICE SHALL BE REMOVED AND DISPOSED OF. THE NPS HAS THE RIGHT TO RETAIN USABLE TILES. NEW TILES MATCHING EXISTING OR A CLOSE AS REASONABLY POSSIBLE SHALL BE INSTALLED WITHIN THE RESOURCE PROTECTION OFFICE. THE EXISTING SUPPORT GRID SHALL BE REUSED. ANY DAMAGES TO THE SUPPORT GRID RESULTING FROM THE REMOVAL OF CEILING TILES SHALL BE REPAIRED AT NO COST TO THE NPS. 7. CONTRACTOR SHALL DEVELOP A WORK PLAN FOR CONTRACTOR SHALL DEVELOP A WORK PLAN FOR WORK PERFOMRED WITHIN STORAGE \(RM121\), COLLECTION STORAGE \(RM124\) AND ARCHIVE STORAGE \(RM125\). SUBMIT WRITTEN WORK PLAN FOR NPS REVIEW DETAILING ACTIONS AND SAFEGUARD TO PROTECT THE CONTENTS OF THESE ROOMS FOR DAMAGE DURING DEMOLITION AND CONSTRUCTION ACTIVITIES. INCLUDE SAFEGUARDS TO PROTECT FROM DUST AND DEBRIS. CONTINUOUS CLEANING WILL BE REQUIRED. THE USE OF HEPA VACUUM CLEANER SHALL BE REQUIRED.)/Border[0 0 0]/NM(HPXDQUQCWAJGXGCE)/M(D:20250228120642-06'00')/AP<</N 9836 0 R>>/RD[0 0 0 0]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:contentType="text/html" xfa:APIVersion="BluebeamPDFRevu:2018" xfa:spec="2.2.0" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p>1. FIRE-RESISTANT RATED BARRIERS SHALL BE FIRE-RESISTANT RATED BARRIERS SHALL BE MAINTAINED. INSTALL FIRESTOPPING AND JOINT SEALANTS AS REQUIRED FOR NEW THROUGH AND MEMBRANE PENETRATIONS. SEAL ALL PENETRATIONS ABANDONED AS PART OF THE SCOPE OF WORK. 2. THE REINFORCED CONCRETE SHEAR WALL MEASURES THE REINFORCED CONCRETE SHEAR WALL MEASURES 24 INCHES THICK. NO NEW THROUGH PENETRATIONS SHALL BE MADE. EXISTING THROUGH PENETRATIONS AND OPENINGS SHALL BE USED. SURFACE MOUNT DEVICE MOUNTING MAY BE ALLOWED WITH NPS PRIOR APPROVAL. 3. CORRIDOR 101 FEATURES A DYE SUBLIMATION CORRIDOR 101 FEATURES A DYE SUBLIMATION PRINTED PVC PHOTOGRAPHIC FLOOR COVERING SUSCEPTIBLE TO MECHANICAL DAMAGE FROM LADDERS, LIFTS, SCAFFOLDING AND DROPPED TOOLS. CONTRACTOR SHALL PROTECT THE ENTIRE FLOOR WITH ROLLED PAPER BOARD PROTECTOR HAVING A MINIMUM THICKNESS OF 40 MIL. OVERLAP SEAMS BY 6IN AND TAPE SEAMS TOP AND BOTTOM WITH SEAM TAPE SUPPLIED FROM THE SAME MANUFACTURER AS PAPER BOARD. WHERE SELF PROPELLED LIFTS OR SCAFFOLDS ARE USED 1/2IN PLYWOOD PLANKS OR SHEETS SHALL BE PLACED OVER PAPER BOARD TO AFFORD A HIGHER LEVEL OF PROTECTION. 4. COORDINATE ALL WORK WITHIN PUBLIC AREAS COORDINATE ALL WORK WITHIN PUBLIC AREAS \(ROOMS, 100, 101, 102, 103, 105, 106, 111, 112, 113, 114 AND 115\) WITH NPS TO ENSURE THAT WORK DOES NOT IMPACT THE VISITOR'S EXPERIENCE. WORKING AFTER HOURS OR OFF SEASON MAY BE REQUIRED. 5. WORK PERFORMED WITHIN LOWER DISTRICT RESOURCE WORK PERFORMED WITHIN LOWER DISTRICT RESOURCE PROTECTION OFFICES \(RM 119\), STORAGE \(RM 121\), COLLECTION STORAGE \(RM 124\) AND ARCHIVE STORAGE \(RM 125\) MUST BE PERFORMED WITH NPS ESCORT BEING PRESENT. 6. ALL CEILING TILES BROKEN OR OTHERWISE DAMAGED ALL CEILING TILES BROKEN OR OTHERWISE DAMAGED DURING DEMOLITION AND SYSTEM INSTALLATION SHALL BE REMOVED AND REPLACED WITH CEILING TILES TAKEN FROM THE RESOURCE PROTECTION OFFICE \(RM 119 AND 120\). UPON COMPLETION OF DEMOLITION AND INSTALLATION ALL REMAINING CEILING TILES WITHIN THE RESOURCE PROTECTION OFFICE SHALL BE REMOVED AND DISPOSED OF. THE NPS HAS THE RIGHT TO RETAIN USABLE TILES. NEW TILES MATCHING EXISTING OR A CLOSE AS REASONABLY POSSIBLE SHALL BE INSTALLED WITHIN THE RESOURCE PROTECTION OFFICE. THE EXISTING SUPPORT GRID SHALL BE REUSED. ANY DAMAGES TO THE SUPPORT GRID RESULTING FROM THE REMOVAL OF CEILING TILES SHALL BE REPAIRED AT NO COST TO THE NPS. 7. CONTRACTOR SHALL DEVELOP A WORK PLAN FOR CONTRACTOR SHALL DEVELOP A WORK PLAN FOR WORK PERFOMRED WITHIN STORAGE \(RM121\), COLLECTION STORAGE \(RM124\) AND ARCHIVE STORAGE \(RM125\). SUBMIT WRITTEN WORK PLAN FOR NPS REVIEW DETAILING ACTIONS AND SAFEGUARD TO PROTECT THE CONTENTS OF THESE ROOMS FOR DAMAGE DURING DEMOLITION AND CONSTRUCTION ACTIVITIES. INCLUDE SAFEGUARDS TO PROTECT FROM DUST AND DEBRIS. CONTINUOUS CLEANING WILL BE REQUIRED. THE USE OF HEPA VACUUM CLEANER SHALL BE REQUIRED.</p></body>)>>
endobj
