1425 0 obj<</Subtype/Square/Rect[120 1013 455 1526]/T(AutoCAD SHX Text)/F 64/Contents(GENERAL SHEET NOTES: 1. FIRE-RESISTANT RATED BARRIERS SHALL BE FIRE-RESISTANT RATED BARRIERS SHALL BE MAINTAINED. INSTALL FIRESTOPPING AND JOINT SEALANTS AS REQUIRED FOR NEW THROUGH AND MEMBRANE PENETRATIONS. SEAL ALL PENETRATIONS HIGHER AS PART OF THE SCOPE OF WORK. 2. THE REINFORCED CONCRETE SHEAR WALL THE REINFORCED CONCRETE SHEAR WALL MEASURES 24 INCHES THICK. NO NEW THROUGH PENETRATIONS SHALL BE MADE. EXISTING THROUGH PENETRATIONS AND OPENING SHALL BE USED. SURFACE MOUNT DEVICE MOUNTING MAY BE ALLOWED WITH NPS PRIOR APPROVAL. 3. ALL CEILING TILES BROKEN OR OTHERWISE ALL CEILING TILES BROKEN OR OTHERWISE DAMAGED DURING DEMOLITION AND SYSTEM INSTALLATION SHALL BE REMOVED AND REPLACED WITH CEILING TILES TAKEN FROM THE RESOURCE PROTECTION OFFICE \(RM 119 AND 120\). UPON COMPLETION DEMOLITION AND INSTALLATION ALL REMAINING CEILING TILES WITHIN THE RESOURCE PROTECTION OFFICE SHALL BE REMOVED AND DISPOSED OF. THE NPS HAS THE RIGHT TO RETAIN USABLE TILES. NEW TILES MATCHING EXISTING OR A CLOSE AS REASONABLY POSSIBLE OFFICE. THE EXISTING SUPPORT SHALL REUSED. ANY DAMAGES TO THE SUPPORT GRID RESULTING FROM THE REMOVAL OF CEILING TILES SHALL BE REPAIRED AT NO COST TO THE NPS.)/Border[0 0 0]/NM(GRIRADOXODCRKWXQ)/M(D:20250228120643-06'00')/AP<</N 10018 0 R>>/RD[0 0 0 0]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:contentType="text/html" xfa:APIVersion="BluebeamPDFRevu:2018" xfa:spec="2.2.0" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p>GENERAL SHEET NOTES: 1. FIRE-RESISTANT RATED BARRIERS SHALL BE FIRE-RESISTANT RATED BARRIERS SHALL BE MAINTAINED. INSTALL FIRESTOPPING AND JOINT SEALANTS AS REQUIRED FOR NEW THROUGH AND MEMBRANE PENETRATIONS. SEAL ALL PENETRATIONS HIGHER AS PART OF THE SCOPE OF WORK. 2. THE REINFORCED CONCRETE SHEAR WALL THE REINFORCED CONCRETE SHEAR WALL MEASURES 24 INCHES THICK. NO NEW THROUGH PENETRATIONS SHALL BE MADE. EXISTING THROUGH PENETRATIONS AND OPENING SHALL BE USED. SURFACE MOUNT DEVICE MOUNTING MAY BE ALLOWED WITH NPS PRIOR APPROVAL. 3. ALL CEILING TILES BROKEN OR OTHERWISE ALL CEILING TILES BROKEN OR OTHERWISE DAMAGED DURING DEMOLITION AND SYSTEM INSTALLATION SHALL BE REMOVED AND REPLACED WITH CEILING TILES TAKEN FROM THE RESOURCE PROTECTION OFFICE \(RM 119 AND 120\). UPON COMPLETION DEMOLITION AND INSTALLATION ALL REMAINING CEILING TILES WITHIN THE RESOURCE PROTECTION OFFICE SHALL BE REMOVED AND DISPOSED OF. THE NPS HAS THE RIGHT TO RETAIN USABLE TILES. NEW TILES MATCHING EXISTING OR A CLOSE AS REASONABLY POSSIBLE OFFICE. THE EXISTING SUPPORT SHALL REUSED. ANY DAMAGES TO THE SUPPORT GRID RESULTING FROM THE REMOVAL OF CEILING TILES SHALL BE REPAIRED AT NO COST TO THE NPS.</p></body>)>>
endobj
