1840 0 obj<</Subtype/Square/Rect[129 894 594 1167]/T(AutoCAD SHX Text)/F 64/Contents(5. ALL CEILING TILES BROKEN OR OTHERWISE DAMAGED DURING ALL CEILING TILES BROKEN OR OTHERWISE DAMAGED DURING DEMOLITION AND SYSTEM INSTALLATION SHALL BE REMOVED AND REPLACED WITH CEILING TILES TAKEN FROM THE RESOURCE PROTECTION OFFICE \(RMS 119 AND 120\). UPON COMPLETION OF DEMOLITION AND INSTALLATION ALL REMAINING CEILING TILES WITHIN THE RESOURCE PROTECTION OFFICE SHALL BE REMOVED AND DISPOSED OF. THE NPS HAS THE RIGHT TO RETAIN USABLE TILES. NEW TILES MATCHING EXISTING OR AS CLOSE AS REASONABLY POSSIBLE SHALL BE INSTALLED WITHIN THE RESOURCE PROTECTION OFFICE. THE EXISTING SUPPORT GRID SHALL BE REUSED. ANY DAMAGES TO THE SUPPORT GRID RESULTING FROM THE REMOVAL OF CEILING TILES SHALL BE REPAIRED AT NO COST TO THE NPS. 6. AT THE TIME OF THE SITE SURVEY, MULTIPLE SPARE CIRCUITS WERE AT THE TIME OF THE SITE SURVEY, MULTIPLE SPARE CIRCUITS WERE AVAILABLE ON ELECTRICAL PANELS 1 AND 3. CONTRACTOR SHALL USE THESE ELECTRICAL PANELS TO POWER FIRE ALARM, INTRUSION ALARM, ELECTRONIC ACCESS CONTROL, AND VIDEO SURVEILLANCE EQUIPMENT. )/Border[0 0 0]/NM(AQDHVQDKERKLSAMS)/M(D:20250228120643-06'00')/AP<</N 10393 0 R>>/RD[0 0 0 0]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:contentType="text/html" xfa:APIVersion="BluebeamPDFRevu:2018" xfa:spec="2.2.0" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p>5. ALL CEILING TILES BROKEN OR OTHERWISE DAMAGED DURING ALL CEILING TILES BROKEN OR OTHERWISE DAMAGED DURING DEMOLITION AND SYSTEM INSTALLATION SHALL BE REMOVED AND REPLACED WITH CEILING TILES TAKEN FROM THE RESOURCE PROTECTION OFFICE \(RMS 119 AND 120\). UPON COMPLETION OF DEMOLITION AND INSTALLATION ALL REMAINING CEILING TILES WITHIN THE RESOURCE PROTECTION OFFICE SHALL BE REMOVED AND DISPOSED OF. THE NPS HAS THE RIGHT TO RETAIN USABLE TILES. NEW TILES MATCHING EXISTING OR AS CLOSE AS REASONABLY POSSIBLE SHALL BE INSTALLED WITHIN THE RESOURCE PROTECTION OFFICE. THE EXISTING SUPPORT GRID SHALL BE REUSED. ANY DAMAGES TO THE SUPPORT GRID RESULTING FROM THE REMOVAL OF CEILING TILES SHALL BE REPAIRED AT NO COST TO THE NPS. 6. AT THE TIME OF THE SITE SURVEY, MULTIPLE SPARE CIRCUITS WERE AT THE TIME OF THE SITE SURVEY, MULTIPLE SPARE CIRCUITS WERE AVAILABLE ON ELECTRICAL PANELS 1 AND 3. CONTRACTOR SHALL USE THESE ELECTRICAL PANELS TO POWER FIRE ALARM, INTRUSION ALARM, ELECTRONIC ACCESS CONTROL, AND VIDEO SURVEILLANCE EQUIPMENT. </p></body>)>>
endobj
