2473 0 obj<</Subtype/Square/Rect[1911 1072 2362 1498]/T(AutoCAD SHX Text)/F 64/Contents(PROVIDE 120VAC, 15,000 MINIMUM LUMEN, FULL CUT OFF, LED WALL PACK WITH PHOTOELECTRIC SENSOR, OCCUPANCY SENSOR, AND STEP-DIMMING DRIVER THAT WILL DIM FIXTURES TO 50% WHEN NO OCCUPANCY IS DETECTED. PLACE FIXTURE AT 15 FT AFF OR AS HIGH AS BUILDING WILL ALLOW. UTILIZE SPACES IN EXISTING PANEL TO PROVIDE POWER TO NEW WALL PACK LUMINAIRES. PROVIDE EACH CIRCUIT WITH A NEW 20/1 BREAKER TO MATCH EXISTING.  ALL CIRCUITS SHOULD USE #12 COPPER CONDUCTORS IN 3/4" CONDUIT. CONTRACTOR TO RECONFIGURE AND RE-USE EXITING CIRCUIT FOR ALARM CONTROL UNIT.  COORDINATE WITH THE FIRE ALARM AND INTRUSION ALARM CONTRACTOR.  PROVIDE EACH CIRCUIT WITH A NEW 20/1 BREAKER TO MATCH EXISTING.   UTILIZE SPACES IN EXISTING PANELS TO PROVIDE POWER TO ALARM SYSTEM AUXILIARY POWER SUPPLIES, ACCESS CONTROL SYSTEM, LOCKING HARDWARE POWER SUPPLIES, CAMERA HEATER/BLOWER POWER SUPPLIES, ETC.  NOT ALL EQUIPMENT IS SHOWN, AS EQUIPMENT QUANTITIES AND LOCATIONS WILL BE DETERMINED BY THE FIRE/INTRUSION ALARM SYSTEM, ACCESS CONTROL SYSTEM AND VIDEO SURVEILLANCE SYSTEM CONTRACTOR.  COORDINATE WITH THE FIRE/INTRUSION ALARM SYSTEM, ACCESS CONTROL SYSTEM AND VIDEO SURVEILLANCE SYSTEM CONTRACTOR.  ALL CIRCUITS SHOULD USE #12 COPPER CONDUCTORS IN 3/4" CONDUIT.  PROVIDE EACH CIRCUIT WITH A NEW 20/1 BREAKER TO MATCH EXISTING.  )/Border[0 0 0]/NM(PKXNXVUFFJXTFNLU)/M(D:20250228120643-06'00')/AP<</N 10787 0 R>>/RD[0 0 0 0]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:contentType="text/html" xfa:APIVersion="BluebeamPDFRevu:2018" xfa:spec="2.2.0" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p>PROVIDE 120VAC, 15,000 MINIMUM LUMEN, FULL CUT OFF, LED WALL PACK WITH PHOTOELECTRIC SENSOR, OCCUPANCY SENSOR, AND STEP-DIMMING DRIVER THAT WILL DIM FIXTURES TO 50% WHEN NO OCCUPANCY IS DETECTED. PLACE FIXTURE AT 15 FT AFF OR AS HIGH AS BUILDING WILL ALLOW. UTILIZE SPACES IN EXISTING PANEL TO PROVIDE POWER TO NEW WALL PACK LUMINAIRES. PROVIDE EACH CIRCUIT WITH A NEW 20/1 BREAKER TO MATCH EXISTING.  ALL CIRCUITS SHOULD USE #12 COPPER CONDUCTORS IN 3/4" CONDUIT. CONTRACTOR TO RECONFIGURE AND RE-USE EXITING CIRCUIT FOR ALARM CONTROL UNIT.  COORDINATE WITH THE FIRE ALARM AND INTRUSION ALARM CONTRACTOR.  PROVIDE EACH CIRCUIT WITH A NEW 20/1 BREAKER TO MATCH EXISTING.   UTILIZE SPACES IN EXISTING PANELS TO PROVIDE POWER TO ALARM SYSTEM AUXILIARY POWER SUPPLIES, ACCESS CONTROL SYSTEM, LOCKING HARDWARE POWER SUPPLIES, CAMERA HEATER/BLOWER POWER SUPPLIES, ETC.  NOT ALL EQUIPMENT IS SHOWN, AS EQUIPMENT QUANTITIES AND LOCATIONS WILL BE DETERMINED BY THE FIRE/INTRUSION ALARM SYSTEM, ACCESS CONTROL SYSTEM AND VIDEO SURVEILLANCE SYSTEM CONTRACTOR.  COORDINATE WITH THE FIRE/INTRUSION ALARM SYSTEM, ACCESS CONTROL SYSTEM AND VIDEO SURVEILLANCE SYSTEM CONTRACTOR.  ALL CIRCUITS SHOULD USE #12 COPPER CONDUCTORS IN 3/4" CONDUIT.  PROVIDE EACH CIRCUIT WITH A NEW 20/1 BREAKER TO MATCH EXISTING.  </p></body>)>>
endobj
