6659 0 obj<</Subtype/Square/Rect[2028 728 2381 1178]/T(AutoCAD SHX Text)/F 64/Contents(1. ASBESTOS AWARENESS: TESTING FOR ASBESTOS HAS ASBESTOS AWARENESS: TESTING FOR ASBESTOS HAS NOT BEEN PERFORMED WITHIN THE BUILDING'S OF THIS PROJECT. ASBESTOS CONTAINING MATERIALS \(ACM\) CAN BE PRESENT WITHIN OLDER BUILDING MATERIALS AND THE CONTRACTOR IS HEREBY ADVISED THAT A POTENTIAL FOR ASBESTOS HAZARD EXISTS. THE CONTRACTOR, AT HIS/HER DISCRETION, MAY PERFORM SPOT-TESTING OR OTHER MEANS TO IDENTIFY ACM WHERE DEMOLITION OR CONSTRUCTION IS DESIRABLE, OR PRIOR TO ANY EMPLOYEE TASK THAT MIGHT SUBJECT WORKERS TO ASBESTOS HAZARDS. IF ACM IS DISCOVERED, CONTACT THE GOVERNMENT REPRESENTATIVE AND COMPLY WITH OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY AND HEALTH ADMINISTRATION \(OSHA\) 29 CFR 1926.1101. THIS REGULATION REQUIRES THE CONTRACTOR TO DEVELOP WORK STRATEGIES THAT MINIMIZE EXPOSURE TO ASBESTOS HAZARDS.  2. LEAD-BASED PAINT INVESTIGATION AND TESTING HAS LEAD-BASED PAINT INVESTIGATION AND TESTING HAS NOT BEEN PERFORMED ON PAINTED SURFACES IN THE PROJECT AREA FOR LEAD CONTENT. LEAD CAN BE PRESENT IN OLDER PAINTED FINISHES, AND THE CONTRACTOR IS HEREBY ADVISED THAT A POTENTIAL FOR LEAD HAZARD EXISTS. THE CONTRACTOR, AT HIS/HER DISCRETION, MAY EMPLOY CHEMICAL SPOT-TESTING OR OTHER MEANS TO IDENTIFY LEAD COATINGS WHERE MANUAL DEMOLITION IS DESIRABLE, OR PRIOR TO ANY EMPLOYEE TASK THAT MIGHT SUBJECT WORKERS TO LEAD HAZARDS. IF LEAD-BASED PAINT IS DISCOVERED, CONTACT THE GOVERNMENT REPRESENTATIVE AND COMPLY WITH OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY AND HEALTH ADMINISTRATION \(OSHA\) 29 CFR 1926.62. THIS REGULATION REQUIRES THE CONTRACTOR TO DEVELOP WORK STRATEGIES THAT MINIMIZE EXPOSURE TO LEAD HAZARDS.   )/Border[0 0 0]/NM(WOWBGWVIEODFFRFC)/M(D:20250228120642-06'00')/AP<</N 9291 0 R>>/RD[0 0 0 0]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:contentType="text/html" xfa:APIVersion="BluebeamPDFRevu:2018" xfa:spec="2.2.0" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p>1. ASBESTOS AWARENESS: TESTING FOR ASBESTOS HAS ASBESTOS AWARENESS: TESTING FOR ASBESTOS HAS NOT BEEN PERFORMED WITHIN THE BUILDING'S OF THIS PROJECT. ASBESTOS CONTAINING MATERIALS \(ACM\) CAN BE PRESENT WITHIN OLDER BUILDING MATERIALS AND THE CONTRACTOR IS HEREBY ADVISED THAT A POTENTIAL FOR ASBESTOS HAZARD EXISTS. THE CONTRACTOR, AT HIS/HER DISCRETION, MAY PERFORM SPOT-TESTING OR OTHER MEANS TO IDENTIFY ACM WHERE DEMOLITION OR CONSTRUCTION IS DESIRABLE, OR PRIOR TO ANY EMPLOYEE TASK THAT MIGHT SUBJECT WORKERS TO ASBESTOS HAZARDS. IF ACM IS DISCOVERED, CONTACT THE GOVERNMENT REPRESENTATIVE AND COMPLY WITH OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY AND HEALTH ADMINISTRATION \(OSHA\) 29 CFR 1926.1101. THIS REGULATION REQUIRES THE CONTRACTOR TO DEVELOP WORK STRATEGIES THAT MINIMIZE EXPOSURE TO ASBESTOS HAZARDS.  2. LEAD-BASED PAINT INVESTIGATION AND TESTING HAS LEAD-BASED PAINT INVESTIGATION AND TESTING HAS NOT BEEN PERFORMED ON PAINTED SURFACES IN THE PROJECT AREA FOR LEAD CONTENT. LEAD CAN BE PRESENT IN OLDER PAINTED FINISHES, AND THE CONTRACTOR IS HEREBY ADVISED THAT A POTENTIAL FOR LEAD HAZARD EXISTS. THE CONTRACTOR, AT HIS/HER DISCRETION, MAY EMPLOY CHEMICAL SPOT-TESTING OR OTHER MEANS TO IDENTIFY LEAD COATINGS WHERE MANUAL DEMOLITION IS DESIRABLE, OR PRIOR TO ANY EMPLOYEE TASK THAT MIGHT SUBJECT WORKERS TO LEAD HAZARDS. IF LEAD-BASED PAINT IS DISCOVERED, CONTACT THE GOVERNMENT REPRESENTATIVE AND COMPLY WITH OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY AND HEALTH ADMINISTRATION \(OSHA\) 29 CFR 1926.62. THIS REGULATION REQUIRES THE CONTRACTOR TO DEVELOP WORK STRATEGIES THAT MINIMIZE EXPOSURE TO LEAD HAZARDS.   </p></body>)>>
endobj
