endobj
6676 0 obj<</Subtype/Square/Rect[507 823 2393 1505]/T(AutoCAD SHX Text)/F 64/Contents(1. PROVIDE CODE COMPLIANT COMBINED FIRE ALARM AND PROVIDE CODE COMPLIANT COMBINED FIRE ALARM AND INTRUSION ALARM SYSTEM THROUGHOUT EACH BUILDING.  INSTALL FIRE / INTRUSION CONTROL UNIT, REMOTE ANNUNCIATORS \(KEYPADS\), AND NOTIFICATION APPLIANCE CIRCUIT \(NAC\) POWER SUPPLIES AS REQUIRED. PROVIDE MANUAL PULL STATIONS AT ALL EXITS. PROVIDE DUCT SMOKE DETECTION AND HVAC SHUT-DOWN PER NFPA 90A. PROVIDE OCCUPANT NOTIFICATION COMPLYING WITH NFPA 72. ALL WORK SHALL BE INSTALLED IN ACCORDANCE WITH APPLICABLE EDITIONS OF NFPA 70, NFPA 72, INTERNATIONAL BUILDING CODE AND NATIONAL PARK SERVICE \(NPS\) REQUIREMENTS. CERTIFICATE OF FINAL INSPECTION SHALL BE PROVIDED BY THE CONTRACTOR AT COMPLETION OF PROJECT AND PRESENTED TO NPS. 2. FURNISH AND INSTALL COMPLETE FUNTIONAL SYSTEM AS FURNISH AND INSTALL COMPLETE FUNTIONAL SYSTEM AS INDICATED ON CONTRACT DOCUMENTS AND AS EVIDENTLY INTENDED. DRAWINGS ARE DIAGRAMMATIC IN NATURE AND INDICATE GENERAL ARRANGEMENTS OF SYSTEMS AND SCOPE OF WORK. CONTRACTOR SHALL FURNISH AND INSTALL CONDUIT AND WIRING AS REQUIRED ACCOMPLISHING THE FUNCTIONS INTENDED WHETHER SPECIFICALLY SHOWN ON DRAWINGS OR NOT.   3. PLACEMENT OF FIRE ALARM NOTIFICATION CONTROL UNIT PLACEMENT OF FIRE ALARM NOTIFICATION CONTROL UNIT AND WALL MOUNTED DEVICES SHALL BE COORDINATED WITH THE NPS. 4. SMOKE DETECTOR PLACEMENT DETAILED ON DRAWINGS IS SMOKE DETECTOR PLACEMENT DETAILED ON DRAWINGS IS BASED UPON SMOOTH CEILING DESIGN. PLACEMENT OF SMOKE DETECTORS WILL BE DEPENDENT UPON THE ARRANGEMENT OF STRUCTURAL COMPONENTS. THE CONTRACTOR'S DESIGN SHALL TAKE INTO CONSIDERATION STRUCTURAL MEMBERS AND SMOKE DETECTORS SHALL BE PLACED ACCORDINGLY. 5. COORDINATE THE WORK WITH EXISTING CONDITIONS COORDINATE THE WORK WITH EXISTING CONDITIONS INCLUDING SHELVING, CABINETS, FURNITURE, DISPLAY CASES, AUDIO/VISUAL EQUIPMENT, ETC. RESOLVE ALL CONFLICTS THROUGH THE A/E PRIOR TO INSTALLATION.  FAILURE TO COORDINATE WORK WITH EXISTING CONDITIONS, A/E AND NPS SHALL NOT BE CAUSE FOR ADDITIONAL COMPENSATION AND MAY RESULT IN REJECTION OF CONTRACTOR'S WORK. 6. THE QUANTITY AND PLACEMENT OF VISUAL NOTIFICATION THE QUANTITY AND PLACEMENT OF VISUAL NOTIFICATION DEVICES IS DEPENDENT UPON CANDELA RATING. DEVICE PLACEMENT SHOULD BE BASED UPON NFPA 72 CHAPTER 18.5.5. 7. FIRE / INTRUSION ALARM CONTROL UNIT SHALL TRANSMIT FIRE / INTRUSION ALARM CONTROL UNIT SHALL TRANSMIT SIGNALS TO THE REMOTE MONITORING CENTER OF THE NPS' CHOICE VIA DIGITAL COMMUNICATOR, WIRELESS TRANSMITTER, OR CELLULAR RADIO AS REQUIED BY THE NPS. 8. WEATHERPROOF DEVICES SHALL BE PROVIDED AS WEATHERPROOF DEVICES SHALL BE PROVIDED AS REQUIRED, BASED UPON OCCUPANCY AND ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS OF THE SPACE OR AS NOTED ON DRAWINGS. ALL EXTERIOR EQUIPMENT SHALL BE LISTED FOR USE IN THE EXTREME WINTER CONDITIONS OBSERVED WITHIN THE NORTHERN MINNESOTA AND WESTERN WISCONSIN CLIMATE. ELECTRONIC CONTROL EQUIPMENT, POWER SUPPLIES, WIRELESS TRANSMITTER, WIRELESS RECEIVERS, ETC. INSTALLED WITHIN BUILDINGS HAVING NO HEAT OR ON BUILDING EXTERIORS SHALL BE INSTALLED WITHIN NON-METALLIC HEATED AND VENTILATED ELECTRICAL ENCLOSURES. 9. WEATHERPROOF DEVICES SHALL BE PROVIDED FOR WEATHERPROOF DEVICES SHALL BE PROVIDED FOR UNCONDITIONED SPACES SUCH AS ATTICS, CRAWL SPACES, BASEMENTS AND MAINTENANCE SHOP BAYS. DEVICES SHALL BE UL-LISTED FOR THE ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS PRESENT. ADDRESSABLE MODULES OR ELECTRONIC INTERFACE EQUIPMENT MONITORING WEATHERPROOF MANUAL PULL STATIONS, HEAT DETECTORS, ETC. SHALL BE INSTALLED WITHIN ENVIRONMENTALLY CONDITIONED SPACES. 10. MATERIALS SHALL BE NEW AND SUITABLE FOR THE MATERIALS SHALL BE NEW AND SUITABLE FOR THE APPLICATION INTENDED. MATERIALS SHALL BEAR LABELS OR MARKINGS INDICATING THIRD PARTY TESTING LABORATORY LISTINGS ACCEPTABLE TO AUTHORITY HAVING JURISDICTION. 11. EXISTING CABLE, CONDUIT AND SURFACE MOUNTED EXISTING CABLE, CONDUIT AND SURFACE MOUNTED RACEWAY SHALL BE REUSED TO THE FULLEST EXTENT POSSIBLE. FOR NEW AND RELOCATED DEVICES INSTALL NEW CABLE, CONDUIT OR SURFACE MOUNT RACEWAY AS REQUIRED. CABLE SHOULD BE INSTALLED IN METALLIC RACEWAYS. SURFACE MOUNTED RACEWAY SHALL MATCH EXISTING STYLE AND FINISH.  WITHIN FINISHED SPACES, PAINT METALIC CONDUIT TO MATCH EXISTING CONDUIT.   12. PROVIDE PULL AND JUNCTION BOXES AS REQUIRED TO PROVIDE PULL AND JUNCTION BOXES AS REQUIRED TO MEET CODE AND INSTALLATION REQUIREMENTS. PULL AND JUNCTION BOXES SHALL BE CONCEALED IN FINISHED SPACES AND LOCATIONS SHALL BE COORDINATED WITH THE A/E AND NPS TO AVOID CONFLICTS. 13. RACEWAY SHALL BE CONCEALED IN FINISHED SPACES, RACEWAY SHALL BE CONCEALED IN FINISHED SPACES, AND MAY BE EXPOSED IN UNFINISHED SPACES SUCH AS MECHANICAL AND ELECTRICAL ROOMS. RACEWAY SHALL BE RUN PERPENDICULAR OR PARALLEL TO THE BUILDING'S STRUCTURAL COMPONENTS.   14. EXISTING WIRING SHALL BE MEGGER TESTED TO ENSURE EXISTING WIRING SHALL BE MEGGER TESTED TO ENSURE WIRING IS FREE FROM GROUNDS OPENS AND SHORTS.   15. CONDUCTORS SHALL BE IDENTIFIED AT EACH JUNCTION CONDUCTORS SHALL BE IDENTIFIED AT EACH JUNCTION BOX, OUTLET BOX, CABINET, ETC., WITH VINYL SELF-ADHESIVE TAGS INDICATING PANEL AND CIRCUIT NUMBER AND OTHER APPROPRIATE INFORMATION. JUNCTION BOXES SHALL BE LABELED AS TO FUNCTION. WHERE EMPTY RACEWAY IS INSTALLED, IT SHALL BE LABELED AT BOTH ENDS AND FITTED WITH NYLON PULLSTRINGS FOR FUTURE USE. 16. EQUIPMENT SHALL BE SECURELY FASTENED TO MAINTAIN EQUIPMENT SHALL BE SECURELY FASTENED TO MAINTAIN ALIGNMENT AND PREVENT EQUIPMENT MOVEMENT.   17. PENETRATIONS OF FIRE OR SMOKE RATED CONSTRUCTION PENETRATIONS OF FIRE OR SMOKE RATED CONSTRUCTION SHALL BE SEALED WITH FIRESTOPPING MATERIALS APPROVED AND LISTED FOR THE RATING OF THE CONSTRUCTION PENETRATED. PROVIDE DOCUMENTATION ON SUCH PENETRATION SEALING SYSTEMS FOR VERIFICATION OF PROPER INSTALLATION.   18. ALL PENETRATIONS OF ROOFS, EXTERIOR WALLS, ALL PENETRATIONS OF ROOFS, EXTERIOR WALLS, FOUNDATIONS, OR OTHER WATER OR MOISTURE PROOF CONSTRUCTION SHALL BE SEALED WITH APPROPRIATE SEALING FITTINGS OR SEALED CONSTRUCTION TO PREVENT THE INTRODUCTION OF MOISTURE INTO THE BUILDING.  19. WORK SHALL BE PERFORMED ON DE-ENERGIZED WORK SHALL BE PERFORMED ON DE-ENERGIZED SYSTEMS ONLY TO PREVENT PERSONNEL INJURY AND POTENTIAL SYSTEM FAILURE.  20. PULL STATIONS SHALL BE LOCATED 48 IN A.F.F AND PULL STATIONS SHALL BE LOCATED 48 IN A.F.F AND WITHIN 5 FT OF EXIT DOOR.   21. WALL MOUNTED FIRE ALARM NOTIFICATION APPLIANCES, WALL MOUNTED FIRE ALARM NOTIFICATION APPLIANCES, EITHER VISUAL, OR COMBINATION AUDIO/VISUAL, SHALL BE LOCATED SUCH THAT THE ENTIRE LENS OF THE VISUAL PORTION IS BETWEEN 80" AND 96" A.F.F. AUDIO ONLY APPLIANCES SHALL BE LOCATED, NOT LESS THAN, 90" A.F.F. TO TOP OF APPLIANCE, OR 6" BELOW CEILING. 22. ALL MOUNTING DIMENSIONS GIVEN ARE TO THE ALL MOUNTING DIMENSIONS GIVEN ARE TO THE CENTERLINE \(CL\) OF THE DEVICE ABOVE FINISHED FLOOR \(AFF\) OR ABOVE FINISHED GRADE \(AFG\) UNLESS OTHERWISE NOTED. 23. FIRE ALARM CONTROL CABINETS, AND OTHER SIMILAR FIRE ALARM CONTROL CABINETS, AND OTHER SIMILAR CABINETS SHALL BE MOUNTED 6' AFF TO THE TOP. 24. PROTECT EXISTING CONDITIONS INCLUDING FINISHES, PROTECT EXISTING CONDITIONS INCLUDING FINISHES, FURNISHINGS, EQUIPMENT AND PERSONAL BELONGINGS FROM DAMAGE. REPAIR EXISTING FINISHES THAT ARE MARRED, SOILED OR DAMAGED DURING CONSTRUCTION. MATCH EXISTING FINISHES WHERE REPAIRS ARE MADE. CONTRACTOR SHALL SECURE THE SERVICES OF QUALIFIED SUBCONTRACTORS TO INSTALL ALL REQUIRED INTERFACES TO ELEVATORS, HVAC EQUIPMENT, DAMPERS, ACCESS CONTROL EQUIPMENT, CCTV SYSTEMS, LOCKING HARDWARE, NPS NETWORK EQUIPMENT AND POWER DISTRIBUTION SYSTEMS. COORDINATE AND OBTAIN CONTACT INFORMATION FROM NPS FOR EQUIPMENT COVERED UNDER A SERVICE CONTRACTS. 25. PROVIDE DEDICATED 120 VAC FOR ALL FIRE AND PROVIDE DEDICATED 120 VAC FOR ALL FIRE AND INTRUSION ALARM CONTROL EQUIPMENT INCLUDING FIRE AND INTRUSION ALARM CONTROL UNIT, REMOTE CONTROL UNITS, NOTIFICATION APPLIANCE POWER SUPPLIES, ETC. BREAKERS FOR DEDICATED 120 VAC CIRCUITS SHALL BE PAINTED RED AND EQUIPPED WITH BREAKER LOCKS.  IDENTIFY THE ELECTRICAL PANEL AND CIRCUIT NUMBER FOR DEDICATED POWER WITHIN EACH PIECE OF CONTROL EQUIPMENT. 26. WITHIN CONTROL EQUIPMENT SEPARATE HIGH VOLTAGE WITHIN CONTROL EQUIPMENT SEPARATE HIGH VOLTAGE WIRING AND LOW VOLTAGE WIRING WITHIN CONTROL EQUIPMENT ENCLOSURES, GUTTER BOXES, J-BOXES, CONDUIT, ETC IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE NATIONAL ELECTRICAL CODE. 30 POWER LIMITED LOW VOLTAGE WIRING AND NON-POWER POWER LIMITED LOW VOLTAGE WIRING AND NON-POWER LIMITED VOLTAGE WIRING SHALL BE SEPARATED WITHIN CONTROL EQUIPMENT ENCLOSURES, GUTTER BOXES, J-BOXES, CONDUIT, ETC IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE NATIONAL ELECTRICAL CODE. 31. WIRING WITHIN CONTROL EQUIPMENT ENCLOSURES SHALL WIRING WITHIN CONTROL EQUIPMENT ENCLOSURES SHALL BE DRESSED WITHIN GUTTER SPACES TO PREVENT SHIFTING AND INTERMIXING OF HIGH VOLTAGE, NON-POWER LIMITED AND POWER LIMITED WIRING FROM EACH OTHER. DRESSING SHALL BE ACCOMPLISHED WITH WIRE TIES SUPPORTED BY LACING BARS, MECHANICALLY ATTACHED CABLE CLIPS, ETC. ADHESIVE MOUNTED CABLE MANAGEMENT SHALL NOT BE PERMITTED. WIRING SHALL NOT BE TIE WRAPPED TO CIRCUIT BOARD STAND-OFFS. 32. EXTERIOR CAMERAS SHALL BE POSITIONED IN A MANNER EXTERIOR CAMERAS SHALL BE POSITIONED IN A MANNER THAT PREVENTS TAMPERING. CAMERAS SHALL BE MOUNTED 12FT ABOVE GROUND ELEVATION OR GREATER. CAMERA SHALL BE MOUNTED IN A MANNER THAT PREVENTS DAMAGE FROM ROOF SNOW SHEDDING. 33. INSTALL AND TERMINATE 120 VAC POWER FOR INSTALL AND TERMINATE 120 VAC POWER FOR FIRE/INTRUSION ALARM SYSTEMS \(FACU, FIACU, IACU, REMOTE POWER SUPPLIES, ETC.\), ACCESS CONTROL SYSTEM EQUIPMENT \(CARD READER CONTROLLERS, LOCK POWER SUPPLIES, ETC.\) AND VIDEO SURVEILLANCE EQUIPMENT \(HEATER/BLOWER POWER SUPPLIES, NETWORK VIDEO RECORDER, ETC., IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE NATIONAL ELECTRICAL CODE. REFER TO ELECTRICAL PLANS, SECURITY SYSTEMS PLANS, INCLUDING RISER SURVEILLANCE SYSTEM CONTRACTOR. INSTALL SUB-PANEL WHERE INSUFFICIENT SPARE CIRCUITS ARE AVAILABLE. )/Border[0 0 0]/NM(UPECSNNXMDHUHIBY)/M(D:20250228120642-06'00')/AP<</N 9274 0 R>>/RD[0 0 0 0]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:contentType="text/html" xfa:APIVersion="BluebeamPDFRevu:2018" xfa:spec="2.2.0" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p>1. PROVIDE CODE COMPLIANT COMBINED FIRE ALARM AND PROVIDE CODE COMPLIANT COMBINED FIRE ALARM AND INTRUSION ALARM SYSTEM THROUGHOUT EACH BUILDING.  INSTALL FIRE / INTRUSION CONTROL UNIT, REMOTE ANNUNCIATORS \(KEYPADS\), AND NOTIFICATION APPLIANCE CIRCUIT \(NAC\) POWER SUPPLIES AS REQUIRED. PROVIDE MANUAL PULL STATIONS AT ALL EXITS. PROVIDE DUCT SMOKE DETECTION AND HVAC SHUT-DOWN PER NFPA 90A. PROVIDE OCCUPANT NOTIFICATION COMPLYING WITH NFPA 72. ALL WORK SHALL BE INSTALLED IN ACCORDANCE WITH APPLICABLE EDITIONS OF NFPA 70, NFPA 72, INTERNATIONAL BUILDING CODE AND NATIONAL PARK SERVICE \(NPS\) REQUIREMENTS. CERTIFICATE OF FINAL INSPECTION SHALL BE PROVIDED BY THE CONTRACTOR AT COMPLETION OF PROJECT AND PRESENTED TO NPS. 2. FURNISH AND INSTALL COMPLETE FUNTIONAL SYSTEM AS FURNISH AND INSTALL COMPLETE FUNTIONAL SYSTEM AS INDICATED ON CONTRACT DOCUMENTS AND AS EVIDENTLY INTENDED. DRAWINGS ARE DIAGRAMMATIC IN NATURE AND INDICATE GENERAL ARRANGEMENTS OF SYSTEMS AND SCOPE OF WORK. CONTRACTOR SHALL FURNISH AND INSTALL CONDUIT AND WIRING AS REQUIRED ACCOMPLISHING THE FUNCTIONS INTENDED WHETHER SPECIFICALLY SHOWN ON DRAWINGS OR NOT.   3. PLACEMENT OF FIRE ALARM NOTIFICATION CONTROL UNIT PLACEMENT OF FIRE ALARM NOTIFICATION CONTROL UNIT AND WALL MOUNTED DEVICES SHALL BE COORDINATED WITH THE NPS. 4. SMOKE DETECTOR PLACEMENT DETAILED ON DRAWINGS IS SMOKE DETECTOR PLACEMENT DETAILED ON DRAWINGS IS BASED UPON SMOOTH CEILING DESIGN. PLACEMENT OF SMOKE DETECTORS WILL BE DEPENDENT UPON THE ARRANGEMENT OF STRUCTURAL COMPONENTS. THE CONTRACTOR'S DESIGN SHALL TAKE INTO CONSIDERATION STRUCTURAL MEMBERS AND SMOKE DETECTORS SHALL BE PLACED ACCORDINGLY. 5. COORDINATE THE WORK WITH EXISTING CONDITIONS COORDINATE THE WORK WITH EXISTING CONDITIONS INCLUDING SHELVING, CABINETS, FURNITURE, DISPLAY CASES, AUDIO/VISUAL EQUIPMENT, ETC. RESOLVE ALL CONFLICTS THROUGH THE A/E PRIOR TO INSTALLATION.  FAILURE TO COORDINATE WORK WITH EXISTING CONDITIONS, A/E AND NPS SHALL NOT BE CAUSE FOR ADDITIONAL COMPENSATION AND MAY RESULT IN REJECTION OF CONTRACTOR'S WORK. 6. THE QUANTITY AND PLACEMENT OF VISUAL NOTIFICATION THE QUANTITY AND PLACEMENT OF VISUAL NOTIFICATION DEVICES IS DEPENDENT UPON CANDELA RATING. DEVICE PLACEMENT SHOULD BE BASED UPON NFPA 72 CHAPTER 18.5.5. 7. FIRE / INTRUSION ALARM CONTROL UNIT SHALL TRANSMIT FIRE / INTRUSION ALARM CONTROL UNIT SHALL TRANSMIT SIGNALS TO THE REMOTE MONITORING CENTER OF THE NPS' CHOICE VIA DIGITAL COMMUNICATOR, WIRELESS TRANSMITTER, OR CELLULAR RADIO AS REQUIED BY THE NPS. 8. WEATHERPROOF DEVICES SHALL BE PROVIDED AS WEATHERPROOF DEVICES SHALL BE PROVIDED AS REQUIRED, BASED UPON OCCUPANCY AND ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS OF THE SPACE OR AS NOTED ON DRAWINGS. ALL EXTERIOR EQUIPMENT SHALL BE LISTED FOR USE IN THE EXTREME WINTER CONDITIONS OBSERVED WITHIN THE NORTHERN MINNESOTA AND WESTERN WISCONSIN CLIMATE. ELECTRONIC CONTROL EQUIPMENT, POWER SUPPLIES, WIRELESS TRANSMITTER, WIRELESS RECEIVERS, ETC. INSTALLED WITHIN BUILDINGS HAVING NO HEAT OR ON BUILDING EXTERIORS SHALL BE INSTALLED WITHIN NON-METALLIC HEATED AND VENTILATED ELECTRICAL ENCLOSURES. 9. WEATHERPROOF DEVICES SHALL BE PROVIDED FOR WEATHERPROOF DEVICES SHALL BE PROVIDED FOR UNCONDITIONED SPACES SUCH AS ATTICS, CRAWL SPACES, BASEMENTS AND MAINTENANCE SHOP BAYS. DEVICES SHALL BE UL-LISTED FOR THE ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS PRESENT. ADDRESSABLE MODULES OR ELECTRONIC INTERFACE EQUIPMENT MONITORING WEATHERPROOF MANUAL PULL STATIONS, HEAT DETECTORS, ETC. SHALL BE INSTALLED WITHIN ENVIRONMENTALLY CONDITIONED SPACES. 10. MATERIALS SHALL BE NEW AND SUITABLE FOR THE MATERIALS SHALL BE NEW AND SUITABLE FOR THE APPLICATION INTENDED. MATERIALS SHALL BEAR LABELS OR MARKINGS INDICATING THIRD PARTY TESTING LABORATORY LISTINGS ACCEPTABLE TO AUTHORITY HAVING JURISDICTION. 11. EXISTING CABLE, CONDUIT AND SURFACE MOUNTED EXISTING CABLE, CONDUIT AND SURFACE MOUNTED RACEWAY SHALL BE REUSED TO THE FULLEST EXTENT POSSIBLE. FOR NEW AND RELOCATED DEVICES INSTALL NEW CABLE, CONDUIT OR SURFACE MOUNT RACEWAY AS REQUIRED. CABLE SHOULD BE INSTALLED IN METALLIC RACEWAYS. SURFACE MOUNTED RACEWAY SHALL MATCH EXISTING STYLE AND FINISH.  WITHIN FINISHED SPACES, PAINT METALIC CONDUIT TO MATCH EXISTING CONDUIT.   12. PROVIDE PULL AND JUNCTION BOXES AS REQUIRED TO PROVIDE PULL AND JUNCTION BOXES AS REQUIRED TO MEET CODE AND INSTALLATION REQUIREMENTS. PULL AND JUNCTION BOXES SHALL BE CONCEALED IN FINISHED SPACES AND LOCATIONS SHALL BE COORDINATED WITH THE A/E AND NPS TO AVOID CONFLICTS. 13. RACEWAY SHALL BE CONCEALED IN FINISHED SPACES, RACEWAY SHALL BE CONCEALED IN FINISHED SPACES, AND MAY BE EXPOSED IN UNFINISHED SPACES SUCH AS MECHANICAL AND ELECTRICAL ROOMS. RACEWAY SHALL BE RUN PERPENDICULAR OR PARALLEL TO THE BUILDING'S STRUCTURAL COMPONENTS.   14. EXISTING WIRING SHALL BE MEGGER TESTED TO ENSURE EXISTING WIRING SHALL BE MEGGER TESTED TO ENSURE WIRING IS FREE FROM GROUNDS OPENS AND SHORTS.   15. CONDUCTORS SHALL BE IDENTIFIED AT EACH JUNCTION CONDUCTORS SHALL BE IDENTIFIED AT EACH JUNCTION BOX, OUTLET BOX, CABINET, ETC., WITH VINYL SELF-ADHESIVE TAGS INDICATING PANEL AND CIRCUIT NUMBER AND OTHER APPROPRIATE INFORMATION. JUNCTION BOXES SHALL BE LABELED AS TO FUNCTION. WHERE EMPTY RACEWAY IS INSTALLED, IT SHALL BE LABELED AT BOTH ENDS AND FITTED WITH NYLON PULLSTRINGS FOR FUTURE USE. 16. EQUIPMENT SHALL BE SECURELY FASTENED TO MAINTAIN EQUIPMENT SHALL BE SECURELY FASTENED TO MAINTAIN ALIGNMENT AND PREVENT EQUIPMENT MOVEMENT.   17. PENETRATIONS OF FIRE OR SMOKE RATED CONSTRUCTION PENETRATIONS OF FIRE OR SMOKE RATED CONSTRUCTION SHALL BE SEALED WITH FIRESTOPPING MATERIALS APPROVED AND LISTED FOR THE RATING OF THE CONSTRUCTION PENETRATED. PROVIDE DOCUMENTATION ON SUCH PENETRATION SEALING SYSTEMS FOR VERIFICATION OF PROPER INSTALLATION.   18. ALL PENETRATIONS OF ROOFS, EXTERIOR WALLS, ALL PENETRATIONS OF ROOFS, EXTERIOR WALLS, FOUNDATIONS, OR OTHER WATER OR MOISTURE PROOF CONSTRUCTION SHALL BE SEALED WITH APPROPRIATE SEALING FITTINGS OR SEALED CONSTRUCTION TO PREVENT THE INTRODUCTION OF MOISTURE INTO THE BUILDING.  19. WORK SHALL BE PERFORMED ON DE-ENERGIZED WORK SHALL BE PERFORMED ON DE-ENERGIZED SYSTEMS ONLY TO PREVENT PERSONNEL INJURY AND POTENTIAL SYSTEM FAILURE.  20. PULL STATIONS SHALL BE LOCATED 48 IN A.F.F AND PULL STATIONS SHALL BE LOCATED 48 IN A.F.F AND WITHIN 5 FT OF EXIT DOOR.   21. WALL MOUNTED FIRE ALARM NOTIFICATION APPLIANCES, WALL MOUNTED FIRE ALARM NOTIFICATION APPLIANCES, EITHER VISUAL, OR COMBINATION AUDIO/VISUAL, SHALL BE LOCATED SUCH THAT THE ENTIRE LENS OF THE VISUAL PORTION IS BETWEEN 80" AND 96" A.F.F. AUDIO ONLY APPLIANCES SHALL BE LOCATED, NOT LESS THAN, 90" A.F.F. TO TOP OF APPLIANCE, OR 6" BELOW CEILING. 22. ALL MOUNTING DIMENSIONS GIVEN ARE TO THE ALL MOUNTING DIMENSIONS GIVEN ARE TO THE CENTERLINE \(CL\) OF THE DEVICE ABOVE FINISHED FLOOR \(AFF\) OR ABOVE FINISHED GRADE \(AFG\) UNLESS OTHERWISE NOTED. 23. FIRE ALARM CONTROL CABINETS, AND OTHER SIMILAR FIRE ALARM CONTROL CABINETS, AND OTHER SIMILAR CABINETS SHALL BE MOUNTED 6' AFF TO THE TOP. 24. PROTECT EXISTING CONDITIONS INCLUDING FINISHES, PROTECT EXISTING CONDITIONS INCLUDING FINISHES, FURNISHINGS, EQUIPMENT AND PERSONAL BELONGINGS FROM DAMAGE. REPAIR EXISTING FINISHES THAT ARE MARRED, SOILED OR DAMAGED DURING CONSTRUCTION. MATCH EXISTING FINISHES WHERE REPAIRS ARE MADE. CONTRACTOR SHALL SECURE THE SERVICES OF QUALIFIED SUBCONTRACTORS TO INSTALL ALL REQUIRED INTERFACES TO ELEVATORS, HVAC EQUIPMENT, DAMPERS, ACCESS CONTROL EQUIPMENT, CCTV SYSTEMS, LOCKING HARDWARE, NPS NETWORK EQUIPMENT AND POWER DISTRIBUTION SYSTEMS. COORDINATE AND OBTAIN CONTACT INFORMATION FROM NPS FOR EQUIPMENT COVERED UNDER A SERVICE CONTRACTS. 25. PROVIDE DEDICATED 120 VAC FOR ALL FIRE AND PROVIDE DEDICATED 120 VAC FOR ALL FIRE AND INTRUSION ALARM CONTROL EQUIPMENT INCLUDING FIRE AND INTRUSION ALARM CONTROL UNIT, REMOTE CONTROL UNITS, NOTIFICATION APPLIANCE POWER SUPPLIES, ETC. BREAKERS FOR DEDICATED 120 VAC CIRCUITS SHALL BE PAINTED RED AND EQUIPPED WITH BREAKER LOCKS.  IDENTIFY THE ELECTRICAL PANEL AND CIRCUIT NUMBER FOR DEDICATED POWER WITHIN EACH PIECE OF CONTROL EQUIPMENT. 26. WITHIN CONTROL EQUIPMENT SEPARATE HIGH VOLTAGE WITHIN CONTROL EQUIPMENT SEPARATE HIGH VOLTAGE WIRING AND LOW VOLTAGE WIRING WITHIN CONTROL EQUIPMENT ENCLOSURES, GUTTER BOXES, J-BOXES, CONDUIT, ETC IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE NATIONAL ELECTRICAL CODE. 30 POWER LIMITED LOW VOLTAGE WIRING AND NON-POWER POWER LIMITED LOW VOLTAGE WIRING AND NON-POWER LIMITED VOLTAGE WIRING SHALL BE SEPARATED WITHIN CONTROL EQUIPMENT ENCLOSURES, GUTTER BOXES, J-BOXES, CONDUIT, ETC IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE NATIONAL ELECTRICAL CODE. 31. WIRING WITHIN CONTROL EQUIPMENT ENCLOSURES SHALL WIRING WITHIN CONTROL EQUIPMENT ENCLOSURES SHALL BE DRESSED WITHIN GUTTER SPACES TO PREVENT SHIFTING AND INTERMIXING OF HIGH VOLTAGE, NON-POWER LIMITED AND POWER LIMITED WIRING FROM EACH OTHER. DRESSING SHALL BE ACCOMPLISHED WITH WIRE TIES SUPPORTED BY LACING BARS, MECHANICALLY ATTACHED CABLE CLIPS, ETC. ADHESIVE MOUNTED CABLE MANAGEMENT SHALL NOT BE PERMITTED. WIRING SHALL NOT BE TIE WRAPPED TO CIRCUIT BOARD STAND-OFFS. 32. EXTERIOR CAMERAS SHALL BE POSITIONED IN A MANNER EXTERIOR CAMERAS SHALL BE POSITIONED IN A MANNER THAT PREVENTS TAMPERING. CAMERAS SHALL BE MOUNTED 12FT ABOVE GROUND ELEVATION OR GREATER. CAMERA SHALL BE MOUNTED IN A MANNER THAT PREVENTS DAMAGE FROM ROOF SNOW SHEDDING. 33. INSTALL AND TERMINATE 120 VAC POWER FOR INSTALL AND TERMINATE 120 VAC POWER FOR FIRE/INTRUSION ALARM SYSTEMS \(FACU, FIACU, IACU, REMOTE POWER SUPPLIES, ETC.\), ACCESS CONTROL SYSTEM EQUIPMENT \(CARD READER CONTROLLERS, LOCK POWER SUPPLIES, ETC.\) AND VIDEO SURVEILLANCE EQUIPMENT \(HEATER/BLOWER POWER SUPPLIES, NETWORK VIDEO RECORDER, ETC., IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE NATIONAL ELECTRICAL CODE. REFER TO ELECTRICAL PLANS, SECURITY SYSTEMS PLANS, INCLUDING RISER SURVEILLANCE SYSTEM CONTRACTOR. INSTALL SUB-PANEL WHERE INSUFFICIENT SPARE CIRCUITS ARE AVAILABLE. </p></body>)>>
