6677 0 obj<</Subtype/Square/Rect[117 1505 476 1520]/T(AutoCAD SHX Text)/F 64/Contents(FIRE AND INTRUSION ALARM SYSTEM DEMO GENERAL NOTES:)/Border[0 0 0]/NM(MVYTXKFTAUFABJDU)/M(D:20250228120642-06'00')/AP<</N 9273 0 R>>/RD[0 0 0 0]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:contentType="text/html" xfa:APIVersion="BluebeamPDFRevu:2018" xfa:spec="2.2.0" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p>FIRE AND INTRUSION ALARM SYSTEM DEMO GENERAL NOTES:</p></body>)>>
endobj
6678 0 obj<</Subtype/Square/Rect[120 716 491 1503]/T(AutoCAD SHX Text)/F 64/Contents(1. THE EXISTING CONDITIONS AND DEMOLITION PLANS WERE THE EXISTING CONDITIONS AND DEMOLITION PLANS WERE DEVELOPED BASE ON AVAILABLE AS-BUILT DRAWING AND LIMITED FIELD OBSERVATIONS.  CONTRACTOR SHALL ALLOW FOR VARIANCE IN DEVICES DEPICTED ON DEMOLITION DRAWINGS AND UNFORESEEN CONDITIONS.  2. ALL DEMOLITION WORK IS TO BE COORDINATED WITH NEW ALL DEMOLITION WORK IS TO BE COORDINATED WITH NEW WORK. IF UNDOCUMENTED CONDITION EXIST THAT ARE AFFECTED BY NOTED DEMOLITION, CONTACT THE CONTRACTING OFFICER BEFORE PROCEEDING.  3. THE NATIONAL PARK SERVICE \(NPS\) WILL HAVE FIRST THE NATIONAL PARK SERVICE \(NPS\) WILL HAVE FIRST RIGHTS OF REFUSAL TO ALL EQUIPMENT REMOVED AS PART OF THIS PROJECT. ANYTHING NOT TAKEN BY THE NPS SHALL BE PROPERLY DISPOSED OF OR RECYCLED BY THE CONTRACTOR.  4. THE DEMOLITION OF THE EXISTING FIRE AND INTRUSION THE DEMOLITION OF THE EXISTING FIRE AND INTRUSION ALARM SYSTEM SHALL BE COORDINATED WITH THE NEW FIRE AND INTRUSION ALARM SYSTEM INSTALLATION IN A MANNER THAT REDUCES THE PERIOD OF TIME DURING WHICH A BUILDING REMAINS UNPROTECTED. THE CONTRACTOR SHALL DEVELOP A WORK SCHEDULE AND COORDINATE WITH THE NPS TO ALLOW THE NPS TO SECURE THE SERVICES OF SECURITY PERSONNEL FOR FIREWATCHES AND ASSET PROTECTION AS DEEMED NECESSARY. 5. CONTRACTOR WILL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR PROTECTING ALL CONTRACTOR WILL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR PROTECTING ALL EXISTING CONDITIONS INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO: STRUCTURES, CEILING, WALLS, EQUIPMENT, UTILITIES, ECT. DAMAGE TO EXISTING CONDITIONS WILL BE REPAIRER AT NO ADDITIONAL COST TO THE GOVERNMENT.  6. CONTRACTORS WILL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR PATCHING AND CONTRACTORS WILL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR PATCHING AND REPAIRING FLOOR, CEILINGS AND WALLS TO MATCH EXISTING CONDITIONS IN ALL AREA IMPACTED BY THE DEMOLITION OF THE EXISTING FIRE AND INTRUSION ALARM SYSTEMS AND INSTALLATION OF THE NEW FIRE AND INTRUSION ALARM SYSTEMS. THE USE OF SINGLE AND DOUBLE GANG ELECTRICAL CONVERSE IS ACCEPTABLE FOR FIELD DEVICES WITH SINGLE, DOUBLE, AND 4"X4" BACK-BOX.  7. THE BUILDINGS WILL BE OCCUPIED DURING THE BUILDINGS WILL BE OCCUPIED DURING CONSTRUCTION. THE CONTRACTOR SHALL COORDINATE WORK SCHEDULE WITH NPS PRIOR TO COMMENCING WORK. CONTRACTOR SHALL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR WORKING AROUND OCCUPANT SCHEDULE AS DETERMINED BY THE NPS AND MAINTAIN MINIMUM IMPACT DUE TO CONSTRUCTION. 8. PROTECT ADJACENT MATERIALS INDICATED TO REMAIN. PROTECT ADJACENT MATERIALS INDICATED TO REMAIN. INSTALL AND MAINTAIN DUST AND NOISE BARRIERS TO KEEP DIRT, DUST, AND NOISE FROM BEING TRANSMITTED TO ADJACENT \(UNRENOVATED\) AREAS. REMOVE PROTECTION AND BARRIERS AFTER DEMOLITION OPERATIONS ARE COMPLETE.)/Border[0 0 0]/NM(NAPASGWIRVDRFXYQ)/M(D:20250228120642-06'00')/AP<</N 9272 0 R>>/RD[0 0 0 0]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:contentType="text/html" xfa:APIVersion="BluebeamPDFRevu:2018" xfa:spec="2.2.0" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p>1. THE EXISTING CONDITIONS AND DEMOLITION PLANS WERE THE EXISTING CONDITIONS AND DEMOLITION PLANS WERE DEVELOPED BASE ON AVAILABLE AS-BUILT DRAWING AND LIMITED FIELD OBSERVATIONS.  CONTRACTOR SHALL ALLOW FOR VARIANCE IN DEVICES DEPICTED ON DEMOLITION DRAWINGS AND UNFORESEEN CONDITIONS.  2. ALL DEMOLITION WORK IS TO BE COORDINATED WITH NEW ALL DEMOLITION WORK IS TO BE COORDINATED WITH NEW WORK. IF UNDOCUMENTED CONDITION EXIST THAT ARE AFFECTED BY NOTED DEMOLITION, CONTACT THE CONTRACTING OFFICER BEFORE PROCEEDING.  3. THE NATIONAL PARK SERVICE \(NPS\) WILL HAVE FIRST THE NATIONAL PARK SERVICE \(NPS\) WILL HAVE FIRST RIGHTS OF REFUSAL TO ALL EQUIPMENT REMOVED AS PART OF THIS PROJECT. ANYTHING NOT TAKEN BY THE NPS SHALL BE PROPERLY DISPOSED OF OR RECYCLED BY THE CONTRACTOR.  4. THE DEMOLITION OF THE EXISTING FIRE AND INTRUSION THE DEMOLITION OF THE EXISTING FIRE AND INTRUSION ALARM SYSTEM SHALL BE COORDINATED WITH THE NEW FIRE AND INTRUSION ALARM SYSTEM INSTALLATION IN A MANNER THAT REDUCES THE PERIOD OF TIME DURING WHICH A BUILDING REMAINS UNPROTECTED. THE CONTRACTOR SHALL DEVELOP A WORK SCHEDULE AND COORDINATE WITH THE NPS TO ALLOW THE NPS TO SECURE THE SERVICES OF SECURITY PERSONNEL FOR FIREWATCHES AND ASSET PROTECTION AS DEEMED NECESSARY. 5. CONTRACTOR WILL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR PROTECTING ALL CONTRACTOR WILL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR PROTECTING ALL EXISTING CONDITIONS INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO: STRUCTURES, CEILING, WALLS, EQUIPMENT, UTILITIES, ECT. DAMAGE TO EXISTING CONDITIONS WILL BE REPAIRER AT NO ADDITIONAL COST TO THE GOVERNMENT.  6. CONTRACTORS WILL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR PATCHING AND CONTRACTORS WILL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR PATCHING AND REPAIRING FLOOR, CEILINGS AND WALLS TO MATCH EXISTING CONDITIONS IN ALL AREA IMPACTED BY THE DEMOLITION OF THE EXISTING FIRE AND INTRUSION ALARM SYSTEMS AND INSTALLATION OF THE NEW FIRE AND INTRUSION ALARM SYSTEMS. THE USE OF SINGLE AND DOUBLE GANG ELECTRICAL CONVERSE IS ACCEPTABLE FOR FIELD DEVICES WITH SINGLE, DOUBLE, AND 4"X4" BACK-BOX.  7. THE BUILDINGS WILL BE OCCUPIED DURING THE BUILDINGS WILL BE OCCUPIED DURING CONSTRUCTION. THE CONTRACTOR SHALL COORDINATE WORK SCHEDULE WITH NPS PRIOR TO COMMENCING WORK. CONTRACTOR SHALL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR WORKING AROUND OCCUPANT SCHEDULE AS DETERMINED BY THE NPS AND MAINTAIN MINIMUM IMPACT DUE TO CONSTRUCTION. 8. PROTECT ADJACENT MATERIALS INDICATED TO REMAIN. PROTECT ADJACENT MATERIALS INDICATED TO REMAIN. INSTALL AND MAINTAIN DUST AND NOISE BARRIERS TO KEEP DIRT, DUST, AND NOISE FROM BEING TRANSMITTED TO ADJACENT \(UNRENOVATED\) AREAS. REMOVE PROTECTION AND BARRIERS AFTER DEMOLITION OPERATIONS ARE COMPLETE.</p></body>)>>
endobj
