6873 0 obj<</Subtype/Square/Rect[126 270 473 1510]/T(AutoCAD SHX Text)/F 64/Contents(1. FIRE-RESISTANT RATED BARRIERS SHALL BE FIRE-RESISTANT RATED BARRIERS SHALL BE MAINTAINED. INSTALL FIRESTOPPING AND JOINT SEALANTS AS REQUIRED FOR NEW THROUGH AND MEMBRANE PENETRATIONS. SEAL ALL PENETRATIONS ABANDONED AS PART OF THE SCOPE OF WORK. 2. THE REINFORCED CONCRETE SHEAR WALL MEASURES THE REINFORCED CONCRETE SHEAR WALL MEASURES 24 INCHES THICK. NO NEW THROUGH PENETRATIONS SHALL BE MADE. EXISTING THROUGH PENETRATIONS AND OPENINGS SHALL BE USED. SURFACE MOUNT DEVICE MOUNTING MAY BE ALLOWED WITH NPS PRIOR APPROVAL. 3. FIRE ALARM NOTIFICATION DEVICES SHALL BE 15 FIRE ALARM NOTIFICATION DEVICES SHALL BE 15 CANDELA UNLESS NOTED OTHERWISE. 4. CEILINGS ARE SUSPENDED LIFT OUT CEILINGS UNLESS CEILINGS ARE SUSPENDED LIFT OUT CEILINGS UNLESS OTHERWISE NOTED AS FOLLOWS: 5. CORRIDOR 101 FEATURES A DYE SUBLIMATION CORRIDOR 101 FEATURES A DYE SUBLIMATION PRINTED PVC PHOTOGRAPHIC FLOOR COVERING SUSCEPTIBLE TO MECHANICAL DAMAGE FROM LADDERS, LIFTS, SCAFFOLDING AND DROPPED TOOLS. CONTRACTOR SHALL PROTECT THE ENTIRE FLOOR WITH ROLLED PAPER BOARD PROTECTION HAVING A MINIMUM THICKNESS OF 40 MIL. OVERLAP SEAM BY 6IN AND TAPE SEAMS TOP AND BOTTOM WITH SEAM TAPE SUPPLIES FROM THE SAME MANUFACTURER AS THE PAPER BOARD. WHERE SELF PROPELLED LIFTS OR SCAFFOLDS ARE USED 1/2IN PLYWOOD PLANKS OR SHEETS SHALL BE PLACED OVER PAPER BOARD TO AFFORD A HIGHER LEVEL OF PROTECTION. 6. COORDINATE ALL WORK WITHIN PUBLIC AREAS COORDINATE ALL WORK WITHIN PUBLIC AREAS \(ROOMS 100, 101, 102, 103, 105, 106, 111, 112, 113, 114 AND 115 WITH NPS TO ENSURE THAT WORK DOES NOT IMPACT THE VISITOR'S EXPERIENCE. WORKING AFTER HOURS OR OFF SEASON MAY REQUIRED. 7. WORK PERFORMED WITHIN LOWER DISTRICT RESOURCE WORK PERFORMED WITHIN LOWER DISTRICT RESOURCE PROTECTION OFFICES \(RM119\), STORAGE \(RM121\), COLLECTION STORAGE \(RM124\) AND ARCHIVE STORAGE \(RM125\) MUST BE PERFORMED WITH NPS ESCORT BEING PRESENT. 8. ALL CEILING TILES BROKEN OR OTHERWISE DAMAGED ALL CEILING TILES BROKEN OR OTHERWISE DAMAGED DURING DEMOLITION AND SYSTEM INSTALLATION SHALL BE REMOVED AND REPLACED WITH CEILING TILES TAKEN FROM THE RESOURCE PROTECTION OFFICE \(RMS 119 AND 120\). UPON COMPLETION OF DEMOLITION AND INSTALLATION ALL REMAINING CEILING TILES WITHIN THE RESOURCE PROTECTION OFFICE SHALL BE REMOVED AND DISPOSED OF. THE NPS HAS THE RIGHT TO RETAIN USABLE TILES. NEW TILES MATCHING EXISTING OR AS CLOSE AS REASONABLY POSSIBLE SHALL BE INSTALLED WITHIN THE RESOURCE PROTECTION OFFICE. THE EXISTING SUPPORT GRID SHALL BE REUSED. ANY DAMAGES TO THE SUPPORT GRID RESULTING FROM THE REMOVAL OF CEILING TILES SHALL BE REPAIRED AT NO COST TO THE NPS. 9. CONTRACTOR SHALL DEVELOP A WORK PLAN FOR CONTRACTOR SHALL DEVELOP A WORK PLAN FOR WORK PERFORMED WITHIN STORAGE \(RM 121\), COLLECTION STORAGE \(RM 124\), AND ARCHIVE STORAGE \(RM 125\). SUBMIT WRITTEN WORK PLAN FOR NPS REVIEW DETAILING ACTIONS AND SAFEGUARDS TO PROTECT THE CONTENTS OF THESE ROOMS FOR DAMAGE DURING DEMOLITION AND CONSTRUCTION ACTIVITIES. INCLUDE SAFEGUARDS TO PROTECT FROM DUST AND DEBRIS. CONTINUOUS CLEANING WILL BE REQUIRED. THE USE OF HEPA VACUUM CLEANER SHALL BE REQUIRED. 10. AT THE TIME OF THE SITE SURVEY, MULTIPLE SPARE AT THE TIME OF THE SITE SURVEY, MULTIPLE SPARE CIRCUITS WERE AVAILABLE ON ELECTRICAL PANELS 1 AND 3. CONTRACTOR SHALL USE THESE ELECTRICAL PANELS TO POWER FIRE ALARM, INTRUSION ALARM, ELECTRONIC ACCESS CONTROL, AND VIDEO SURVEILLANCE EQUIPMENT.)/Border[0 0 0]/NM(XKNDTNYXHBKWISQO)/M(D:20250228120643-06'00')/AP<</N 10140 0 R>>/RD[0 0 0 0]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:contentType="text/html" xfa:APIVersion="BluebeamPDFRevu:2018" xfa:spec="2.2.0" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p>1. FIRE-RESISTANT RATED BARRIERS SHALL BE FIRE-RESISTANT RATED BARRIERS SHALL BE MAINTAINED. INSTALL FIRESTOPPING AND JOINT SEALANTS AS REQUIRED FOR NEW THROUGH AND MEMBRANE PENETRATIONS. SEAL ALL PENETRATIONS ABANDONED AS PART OF THE SCOPE OF WORK. 2. THE REINFORCED CONCRETE SHEAR WALL MEASURES THE REINFORCED CONCRETE SHEAR WALL MEASURES 24 INCHES THICK. NO NEW THROUGH PENETRATIONS SHALL BE MADE. EXISTING THROUGH PENETRATIONS AND OPENINGS SHALL BE USED. SURFACE MOUNT DEVICE MOUNTING MAY BE ALLOWED WITH NPS PRIOR APPROVAL. 3. FIRE ALARM NOTIFICATION DEVICES SHALL BE 15 FIRE ALARM NOTIFICATION DEVICES SHALL BE 15 CANDELA UNLESS NOTED OTHERWISE. 4. CEILINGS ARE SUSPENDED LIFT OUT CEILINGS UNLESS CEILINGS ARE SUSPENDED LIFT OUT CEILINGS UNLESS OTHERWISE NOTED AS FOLLOWS: 5. CORRIDOR 101 FEATURES A DYE SUBLIMATION CORRIDOR 101 FEATURES A DYE SUBLIMATION PRINTED PVC PHOTOGRAPHIC FLOOR COVERING SUSCEPTIBLE TO MECHANICAL DAMAGE FROM LADDERS, LIFTS, SCAFFOLDING AND DROPPED TOOLS. CONTRACTOR SHALL PROTECT THE ENTIRE FLOOR WITH ROLLED PAPER BOARD PROTECTION HAVING A MINIMUM THICKNESS OF 40 MIL. OVERLAP SEAM BY 6IN AND TAPE SEAMS TOP AND BOTTOM WITH SEAM TAPE SUPPLIES FROM THE SAME MANUFACTURER AS THE PAPER BOARD. WHERE SELF PROPELLED LIFTS OR SCAFFOLDS ARE USED 1/2IN PLYWOOD PLANKS OR SHEETS SHALL BE PLACED OVER PAPER BOARD TO AFFORD A HIGHER LEVEL OF PROTECTION. 6. COORDINATE ALL WORK WITHIN PUBLIC AREAS COORDINATE ALL WORK WITHIN PUBLIC AREAS \(ROOMS 100, 101, 102, 103, 105, 106, 111, 112, 113, 114 AND 115 WITH NPS TO ENSURE THAT WORK DOES NOT IMPACT THE VISITOR'S EXPERIENCE. WORKING AFTER HOURS OR OFF SEASON MAY REQUIRED. 7. WORK PERFORMED WITHIN LOWER DISTRICT RESOURCE WORK PERFORMED WITHIN LOWER DISTRICT RESOURCE PROTECTION OFFICES \(RM119\), STORAGE \(RM121\), COLLECTION STORAGE \(RM124\) AND ARCHIVE STORAGE \(RM125\) MUST BE PERFORMED WITH NPS ESCORT BEING PRESENT. 8. ALL CEILING TILES BROKEN OR OTHERWISE DAMAGED ALL CEILING TILES BROKEN OR OTHERWISE DAMAGED DURING DEMOLITION AND SYSTEM INSTALLATION SHALL BE REMOVED AND REPLACED WITH CEILING TILES TAKEN FROM THE RESOURCE PROTECTION OFFICE \(RMS 119 AND 120\). UPON COMPLETION OF DEMOLITION AND INSTALLATION ALL REMAINING CEILING TILES WITHIN THE RESOURCE PROTECTION OFFICE SHALL BE REMOVED AND DISPOSED OF. THE NPS HAS THE RIGHT TO RETAIN USABLE TILES. NEW TILES MATCHING EXISTING OR AS CLOSE AS REASONABLY POSSIBLE SHALL BE INSTALLED WITHIN THE RESOURCE PROTECTION OFFICE. THE EXISTING SUPPORT GRID SHALL BE REUSED. ANY DAMAGES TO THE SUPPORT GRID RESULTING FROM THE REMOVAL OF CEILING TILES SHALL BE REPAIRED AT NO COST TO THE NPS. 9. CONTRACTOR SHALL DEVELOP A WORK PLAN FOR CONTRACTOR SHALL DEVELOP A WORK PLAN FOR WORK PERFORMED WITHIN STORAGE \(RM 121\), COLLECTION STORAGE \(RM 124\), AND ARCHIVE STORAGE \(RM 125\). SUBMIT WRITTEN WORK PLAN FOR NPS REVIEW DETAILING ACTIONS AND SAFEGUARDS TO PROTECT THE CONTENTS OF THESE ROOMS FOR DAMAGE DURING DEMOLITION AND CONSTRUCTION ACTIVITIES. INCLUDE SAFEGUARDS TO PROTECT FROM DUST AND DEBRIS. CONTINUOUS CLEANING WILL BE REQUIRED. THE USE OF HEPA VACUUM CLEANER SHALL BE REQUIRED. 10. AT THE TIME OF THE SITE SURVEY, MULTIPLE SPARE AT THE TIME OF THE SITE SURVEY, MULTIPLE SPARE CIRCUITS WERE AVAILABLE ON ELECTRICAL PANELS 1 AND 3. CONTRACTOR SHALL USE THESE ELECTRICAL PANELS TO POWER FIRE ALARM, INTRUSION ALARM, ELECTRONIC ACCESS CONTROL, AND VIDEO SURVEILLANCE EQUIPMENT.</p></body>)>>
endobj
6874 0 obj<</Subtype/Square/Rect[1931 1015 2382 1090]/T(AutoCAD SHX Text)/F 64/Contents(NEW SPRINKLER SYSTEM WATER FLOW BELL SHALL BE POWERED BY THE FIRE ALARM AUXILIARY POWER AND POWER SWITCHED THROUGH THE DPDT SWITCHES OF THE WET-PIPE WATER FLOW AND DRY-PIPE PRESSURE SWITCH. WATER FLOW BELL SHALL ACT INDEPENDENTLY OF THE FIRE ALARM I/O PROGRAMMING.)/Border[0 0 0]/NM(SJREHBZZXWXSRZWP)/M(D:20250228120643-06'00')/AP<</N 10139 0 R>>/RD[0 0 0 0]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:contentType="text/html" xfa:APIVersion="BluebeamPDFRevu:2018" xfa:spec="2.2.0" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p>NEW SPRINKLER SYSTEM WATER FLOW BELL SHALL BE POWERED BY THE FIRE ALARM AUXILIARY POWER AND POWER SWITCHED THROUGH THE DPDT SWITCHES OF THE WET-PIPE WATER FLOW AND DRY-PIPE PRESSURE SWITCH. WATER FLOW BELL SHALL ACT INDEPENDENTLY OF THE FIRE ALARM I/O PROGRAMMING.</p></body>)>>
